Oh no, there's a whole group of people.

256
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:11,911
I hope they're not those guys from before.

257
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:16,137
Whoever they are, I hope Luffy's
not pulling any of his usual stunts.

258
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:18,277
Let's sit down and take a breather, okay?

259
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:21,419
Zoro, Luffy, Chopper, there's
no reason for us to...

260
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:23,857
Nami, baby!

261
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:24,960
I missed you!

262
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:26,430
Luffy!

263
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:28,991
Promise you won't start any trouble, okay?

264
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:31,357
Don't know if I can keep that promise!

265
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:32,440
Hey, Nami!

266
00:16:32,620 --> 00:16:34,437
We need you to fork up
seven million berries

267
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:36,997
from your stash to pay
for all the fines we got!

268
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:37,910
Oh, good!

269
00:16:37,993 --> 00:16:39,959
So we pay the fine and we're clear!

270
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:43,460
Did he say seven million?

271
00:16:46,820 --> 00:16:47,650
What?

272
00:16:58,180 --> 00:16:59,020
Oh, crap.

273
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:01,837
I was so worked up, I
forgot to hit the brakes.

274
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:02,750
Ouch.

275
00:17:02,940 --> 00:17:03,770
Captain!

276
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:06,337
Hey, thanks for letting
me use your waiver.

277
00:17:06,420 --> 00:17:07,857
I love the way it handles.

278
00:17:07,940 --> 00:17:10,477
I'm glad you enjoyed it,
but more importantly,

279
00:17:10,560 --> 00:17:12,757
do you realize how much
trouble you're in now?

280
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:13,670
Captain!

281
00:17:13,753 --> 00:17:15,517
Guys, let's make ourselves scarce.

282
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:17,897
Aren't you going to finish
the fight you just started?

283
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:21,057
Trust me, this Enaru is not
someone we want to mess with.

284
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:21,970
Yes, quite.

285
00:17:22,140 --> 00:17:25,117
And knocking out an official
is a crime of the fifth degree.

286
00:17:25,200 --> 00:17:28,217
Once you're found guilty of
committing a fifth degree crime,

287
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:31,737
almighty Enaru will banish you to
the land of the drifting clouds.

288
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:32,702
How's that bad?

289
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:34,860
Land of the drifting clouds?

290
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:36,320
That sounds like fun.

291
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:38,920
It's a death sentence. You die!

292
00:17:39,420 --> 00:17:41,777
They'll put you and your
ship on a small cloud.

293
00:17:41,860 --> 00:17:45,457
And set you adrift in the sea with
no chance of rescue or escape.

294
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:49,157
You'll eventually die a
very slow and painful death.

295
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,497
It's terrible.

296
00:17:50,580 --> 00:17:55,020
Interesting that must be why we
saw that ship fall from the sky.

297
00:17:55,620 --> 00:17:56,877
Wait, what are you talking about?

298
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:59,717
Don't you remember that
galleon we saw falling?

299
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:00,737
The saint bris.

300
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:01,737
I think it was called.

301
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:04,997
For all we know that crew could
have been punished over 200.

302
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:06,256
A hundred years ago.

303
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:12,800
You criminals!

304
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:15,617
Do you scum know what
you've done to our captain?

305
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:16,530
Who cares?

306
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:18,217
Sanji, let me handle this.

307
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:19,300
Anything for you!

308
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:20,837
Don't take it so personally.

309
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:22,120
It was a lucky shot.

310
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:23,300
A lucky shot?

311
00:18:24,620 --> 00:18:25,557
Completely unintentional.

312
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:26,700
You're lying!

313
00:18:26,920 --> 00:18:28,497
No, I'm telling you the truth.

314
00:18:28,580 --> 00:18:31,937
Can you blame a beginner for messing
up and nearly killing your boss?

315
00:18:32,020 --> 00:18:32,850
That's weird.

316
00:18:32,933 --> 00:18:34,817
It seemed like you had a
pretty good handle on it to me.

317
00:18:34,900 --> 00:18:35,920
Shut up.

318
00:18:36,120 --> 00:18:37,240
Oh, shit, Luffy.

319
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:40,457
The enemy's trying to trick them
into thinking it was an accident.

320
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:41,716
Don't blow it, okay?

321
00:18:41,980 --> 00:18:42,860
All right.

322
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:46,157
Gentlemen, as important
as your investigation is,

323
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:48,997
perhaps it would be best to get
the captain to a doctor first.

324
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:49,962
Just a thought.

325
00:18:50,160 --> 00:18:51,680
All right, the captain!

326
00:18:52,540 --> 00:18:54,237
Now, there's no reason to panic.

327
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:55,637
Let's take him to my house.

328
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:57,720
We'll get right on that. Let's go.

329
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:03,277
Consider yourselves
under preliminary arrest.

330
00:19:03,360 --> 00:19:04,877
Don't go anywhere. Got it?

331
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:09,637
Why are they crawling again?

332
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:11,697
Can't they just carry
them like normal people?

333
00:19:11,780 --> 00:19:15,857
You guys saved my life, so I know
you're not as bad as they claim you are.

334
00:19:15,940 --> 00:19:18,617
So take this chance and get out of here!

335
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:19,637
Wait!

336
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:23,617
I think we'd better take her advice.

337
00:19:23,700 --> 00:19:28,817
When I was on the waiver, I saw it for
myself: an island filled with monsters.

338
00:19:28,900 --> 00:19:29,837
Right?

339
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:33,037
So you You did exactly what
everyone was hoping you wouldn't do.

340
00:19:33,120 --> 00:19:35,937
You mean the place we were
told to never ever set foot on?

341
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:37,255
And there's monsters?

342
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:39,160
Don't give him any ideas!

343
00:19:39,700 --> 00:19:41,777
It's nothing to get excited about, Luffy.

344
00:19:41,860 --> 00:19:44,257
The last thing we need is
to get involved with this.

345
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:45,477
Regardless, we're leaving.

346
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:46,390
Now let's go!

347
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,577
Ah, it'll break my heart
to be away from Conis,

348
00:19:49,660 --> 00:19:51,597
but if that's what Nami wants, so be it.

349
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:55,877
If we stick around any longer, Conis and
Pakeya may get in trouble because of us.

350
00:19:55,960 --> 00:19:56,790
That's true.

351
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,437
Those white berets will charge
them as our accomplices.

352
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:03,457
If we can escape now on our own, then it
shouldn't cause them any trouble, right?

353
00:20:03,540 --> 00:20:06,317
After all, how can they be helping
us when they're with that captain?

354
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:08,740
Okay, that's the plan. Let's go.

355
00:20:14,460 --> 00:20:15,989
Luffy, what are you doing?

356
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:17,680
Why are we running away?

357
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:19,548
They haven't done anything.

358
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:21,941
Whoever arrests them is an idiot.

359
00:20:26,620 --> 00:20:27,980
Please, please hurry.

360
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:33,140
The Blue Sea Dwellers will never escape.

361
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:38,420
Can't you two argue on the boat? Come on!

362
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:40,477
How many times do I have to tell you?

363
00:20:40,560 --> 00:20:43,420
Staying here equals more
trouble for everybody!

364
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:46,200
We're in trouble no matter what.

365
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:48,340
Save yourselves!

366
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:50,240
Please, go!

367
00:20:50,660 --> 00:20:51,600
Just great.

368
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:52,940
Be careful, miss.

369
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:55,077
If you say anything to
defend these criminals,

370
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:57,984
I will consider you and
your father accomplices.

371
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:01,097
These people must be punished
to the full extent of the

372
00:21:01,180 --> 00:21:04,700
law for all the abusive language
and deplorable violence.

373
00:21:05,340 --> 00:21:08,080
I find them guilty of fifth-degree crimes.

374
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:13,384
In the name of almighty Inaru, you are
banished to drift into clouds for eternity.

375
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:16,460
I told you it was an accident.

376
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:18,200
Oh, forget it.

377
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:19,320
Harass them!

378
00:21:21,020 --> 00:21:23,000
Just run, you can't win.

379
00:21:25,740 --> 00:21:27,760
Fire the milky arrows!

380
00:21:29,480 --> 00:21:31,840
Go, Nami, run, you think?

381
00:21:36,120 --> 00:21:37,397
What the heck?

382
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:38,320
Clouds!

383
00:21:41,680 --> 00:21:43,940
Viper Rays, attack!

384
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:57,400
Cool trick, mind if I try?

385
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:10,580
Whoa, you see his arm?

386
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,720
Look, he's all stretchy.

387
00:22:13,220 --> 00:22:14,220
I hope he's okay.

388
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:22,040
Go away, Devil Fruit!

389
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:25,220
You are worse!

390
00:23:01,080 --> 00:23:02,080
Piece of cake.

391
00:23:03,640 --> 00:23:05,993
Nami, how's the money situation looking?

392
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:08,260
50,000 berries left!

393
00:23:08,380 --> 00:23:09,440
50,000?

394
00:23:09,740 --> 00:23:10,920
Were that broke?

395
00:23:11,140 --> 00:23:13,846
Normally, that'd last
us a day or two at most!

396
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:14,817
What's the deal?

397
00:23:14,900 --> 00:23:16,018
Why are we so poor?

398
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:17,297
Listen up, everybody!

399
00:23:17,380 --> 00:23:18,937
Your captain has something to say!

400
00:23:19,020 --> 00:23:22,137
Everyone on my ship needs to be
more good with money from now on!

401
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:24,040
So lead by example! Huh?

402
00:23:25,020 --> 00:23:29,497
Eh, in any case, the Fighting Formation
B I taught them to use was successful.

403
00:23:29,580 --> 00:23:30,410
There's that.

404
00:23:30,493 --> 00:23:31,323
Really?

405
00:23:31,406 --> 00:23:33,260
They defeated the White Berets.

406
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:35,030
Unbelievable.

407
00:23:35,113 --> 00:23:39,368
At this altitude, the athletic ability
of Blue Sea-Dwellers usually decreases.

408
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:47,917
Those poor deluded fools.

409
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:50,900
Sorry, criminals, you
have no chance of escape!

410
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:55,660
You should have behaved and
done what I told you to do.

411
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:59,360
Of all of the upholders
of law here at Skypiea,

412
00:23:59,820 --> 00:24:02,055
we white parades are the most lenient.

413
00:24:02,620 --> 00:24:05,320
However, they are not nearly as forgiving.

414
00:24:08,760 --> 00:24:09,701
Congratulations!

415
00:24:10,120 --> 00:24:13,040
You are now considered
second-degree criminals.

416
00:24:13,500 --> 00:24:15,880
You can try to cry for mercy,

417
00:24:17,740 --> 00:24:19,920
but you will all be judged?

418
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:24,680
By the priest of Upper Yarn, Hesor!
